  "details": "A minor accessibility / usability annoyance with the visual typewriter indicator at https://wiki.vrchat.com/ during a maintenance, depending on screen reader software and settings used.\n\nExpected markup (line 24):\n\n```\n\n          <p class=\"p with-before output new-output uppercase\" role=\"presentation\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></p>\n\n```\n\nActual markup:\n\n```\n\n          <p class=\"p with-before output new-output uppercase\"></p>\n\n```\n\nAlternatively, the whole block could be replaced with CSS with `::before` and `::after`, but the details of the implementation are out of scope.\n\nExpected result: Always skipped by screen reader software as silent.\n\nActual result: Sometimes read aloud as a \"blank\" line (in NVDA and JAWS according to GLM-5.3-Flash) if not skipped, due to incorrect HTML markup. (Press the P key or Shift+P in NVDA for text paragraph navigation.)",
